{"idx":1,"verdict":"corrected","corrected_claim":"On June 4, 2024 (Lok Sabha counting day), Nifty fell about 8.5% intraday to a low near 21,281 and closed around -5.9% to -6% as the BJP-led NDA looked short of a majority; that night TDP's Chandrababu Naidu and JDU's Nitish Kumar pledged support to form the NDA government. The index recovered over the following months (scaling record highs 32 times in 2024, reaching ~26,000 only in late September 2024), not on the same day.","evidence":[{"title":"Sensex, Nifty plunge 6% after weaker mandate for BJP-led NDA - The Indian Express","url":"https://indianexpress.com/article/business/market/sensex-nifty-plunge-6-after-weaker-mandate-for-bjp-led-nda-9370767/"},{"title":"Nifty 50 set record highs 32 times in 2024, up 11% from June 4 low - Livemint/ht","url":"https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/"},{"title":"Nifty up 2,300 points from June 4 low; when will it hit the 25,000-mark? - Business Standard","url":"https://www.business-standard.com/markets/"}]}
{"idx":2,"verdict":"verified","evidence":[{"title":"HDFC Bank shares plunge 8.5%; stock sees worst day since Covid crash, investors lose Rs 1 lakh crore - The Times of India","url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/hdfc-bank-shares-plunge-8-5-stock-sees-worst-day-since-covid-crash/articleshow/106959118.cms"},{"title":"HDFC Bank sparks worst day for India's Nifty, Sensex since June 2022 - Reuters","url":"https://www.reuters.com/markets/asia/indian-shares-set-open-lower-hdfc-bank-q3-results-hit-sentiment-2024-01-17/"},{"title":"After HDFC Bank results, US Fed signals, markets fall sharpest in 19 months - The Indian Express","url":"https://indianexpress.com/"}]}
{"idx":3,"verdict":"unverifiable","notes":"No reputable source confirmed an April 8, 2026 India-Pakistan ceasefire or a specific Nifty surge to 24,000 on that date; akin to late-March/April 2026 US-Iran ceasefire reports instead.","evidence":[]}
{"idx":4,"verdict":"corrected","corrected_claim":"India overhauled GST slabs effective September 22, 2025: the 28% slab was largely merged into 18%, the 12% slab into 5%, leaving 5% and 18% as the main rates plus a new 40% rate on luxury/demerit goods. The reform was signalled at the August 15 (Independence Day) speech and formalized by the GST Council.","evidence":[{"title":"GST rate cuts from September 22; Relief for Common Man, Boost for Businesses - News On AIR","url":"https://newsonair.gov.in/"},{"title":"New GST regime from Sept 22: 5% and 18% slabs remain, 40% on luxury goods - India Today","url":"https://www.indiatoday.in/"},{"title":"GST tax slab revamp explained: What may get cheaper, costlier and change - Upstox","url":"https://upstox.com/news/"}]}
{"idx":5,"verdict":"corrected","corrected_claim":"In 2019 the government took two separate pro-market steps: (1) August 2, 2019 - rolled back the July 2019 budget's enhanced FPI/investment surcharge (the 'no tax on FPIs' U-turn, via ordinance, after heavy FII selling); (2) September 20, 2019 (a Friday) - slashed corporate tax from 30% to 22% (25.17% effective) for existing companies, sparking the biggest Bank Nifty single-day gain ever (~8%) and a sharp Nifty rally.","evidence":[{"title":"Mini-Budget after Budget: Government slashes corporate tax rates to boost economy - The Times of India","url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/"},{"title":"Nifty Bank index jumps 8%, biggest single-day gain ever - CNBC TV18","url":"https://www.cnbctv18.com/"},{"title":"Government slashes corporate tax to 25.17% for domestic companies - The Times of India","url":"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/"}]}
