{"idx":7,"verdict":"corrected","corrected_claim":"After Hindenburg Research's January 24, 2023 report on the Adani Group, NSE (early February 2023) placed Adani Enterprises, Adani Ports, Ambuja Cement and other Adani firms under the Additional Surveillance Measure (ASM) framework (price banding / extra surveillance, tradeable - not a trading ban); Adani Ports was also put on the F&O ban list for Feb 3, 2023. The Adani Enterprises FPO still closed fully subscribed (backed by institutional bids) even as the stock traded below the FPO price, after which the stock fell sharply (~30%+ from pre-report levels).","evidence":[{"title":"NSE, BSE put Adani Power under short-term additional surveillance measure - Business Today","url":"https://www.businesstoday.in/"},{"title":"Adani Enterprises, Adani Ports And Ambuja Under NSE's Additional Surveillance From Today - NDTV Profit","url":"https://www.ndtvprofit.com/"},{"title":"NSE adds Adani Ports to ban list for February 3 - Moneycontrol","url":"https://www.moneycontrol.com/"}]}
{"idx":8,"verdict":"corrected","corrected_claim":"The Union Budget was presented on February 1, 2020 (a Saturday); on the first trading session after it (Monday, February 3, 2020) Sensex fell about 988 points and Nifty slid below 11,700 (roughly -2.2%), driven by the spreading coronavirus rather than the budget proposals - one of the largest budget-adjacent market falls in a decade.","evidence":[{"title":"Sensex down by 988 points, Nifty below 11,700 on Union Budget day - The Hindu","url":"https://www.thehindu.com/business/markets/"},{"title":"Nifty fall since October 2nd biggest in 10 years; 16 stocks tank over 20% - Business Standard","url":"https://www.business-standard.com/"}]}
